https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5246#section-7.4.1.4.1

TLS 1.2 allowed SHA-224. I cut it from TLS 1.3 in draft 08.

https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-08#section-1.2
https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-08#section-6.3.2.1

I see no reason to treat it as worse than SHA-1, so in the pending PR they're both allowed for fallback chains. SHA-1 and SHA-224 would only be permitted if no better chain could be constructed using known supported algorithms via the "signature_algorithms" extension. (and MD5 should always be considered unacceptable)


Dave


